{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1337676-question-about-the-skeleton-keys-from-new-world-order","id":1337676,"title":"Question about the Skeleton Keys from New World Order","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-24T12:51:55-07:00","id":1337676,"title":"Question about the Skeleton Keys from New World Order","content":"I read the New World Order book and I'm a little confused. Who exactly are the Skeleton Keys and what happened to them after the Grand Housecleaning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T13:19:21-07:00","id":1337683,"title":"","content":"To quote the Revised Convention Book, page 26:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 1886, the activities of Detective Sergeant Crispin and Inspector Rathbone, investigators with Scotland Yard, crossed the desk of financier Reginald Proctor. Rathbone and Crispin\u2019s secret society, the Skeleton Keys, was composed primarily of law-enforcement officers with a mission in line with that of the Technocratic Union.<br /> <br /> These Skeleton Keys, so named for the black keys of membership they carried, were devoted to the investigation and eradication of preternatural threats. </div> </div> </div>Though their mission was in line with the Technocracy's, the Skeleton Keys had arisen independently of them and the Traditions. The relative proportions of those who were Sleepers, Extraordinary Citizens, and Enlightened is unknown.<br /> <br /> NWO history is a bit contradictory on what happened to them: Guide to the Technocracy says they renamed themselves the Ivory Tower, becoming the predecessors to the NWO; the Revised Convention Book says they were assimilated into the Lightkeepers, who it says were the NWO's predecessors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T14:39:29-07:00","id":1337704,"title":"","content":"Thanks \ud83d\ude0a. I appreciate the info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-24T14:53:52-07:00","id":1337708,"title":"","content":"My presumption has always been that they were a surviving faction of the Ksirafai from Sorcerers' Crusade. But I don't think that has ever been mentioned officially or anything.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, if left to their own devices, they make a really cool counterpart to the modern Project Twilight stuff for Victorian Vampire and other period games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T17:57:53-07:00","id":1338541,"title":"","content":"I like the Ksirafai. They\u2019re cool. I heard somewhere that they\u2019re the ancestors of House Janissary in the Order of Herm\u00e8s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T22:37:07-07:00","id":1338572,"title":"","content":"I think in the current lore for Order of Hermes (The revised book, maybe M20) is that House Janissary got found out that they were mostly Ksirafai, and the Euthanatos screamed and killed most of them and the rest of the Order just kinda played in the dirt and went &quot;hmmm? What house?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-30T01:06:40-07:00","id":1338587,"title":"","content":"Thank you \ud83d\ude0a. That was the impression I got too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}